From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Umair Ahmed Shah <umairahmedshah@hotmail.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Apr 2026 10:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] rz/common/bl2: print the EDGE boot marker during platform setup

When EDGE_BOOT_VERSION is defined at compile time, emit a NOTICE line after the
standard LSI register dump so the build identity is visible on serial
immediately after BL2 platform setup completes.  The marker is injected via
-DEDGE_BOOT_VERSION='"<string>"' in EXTRA_OEMAKE; absent the define the code
compiles away with no overhead.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [local build identification only]

Signed-off-by: Umair Ahmed Shah <umairahmedshah@hotmail.com>
---
 plat/renesas/rz/common/bl2_plat_setup.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/plat/renesas/rz/common/bl2_plat_setup.c b/plat/renesas/rz/common/bl2_plat_setup.c
index edf08cb..f4b1c2d 100644
--- a/plat/renesas/rz/common/bl2_plat_setup.c
+++ b/plat/renesas/rz/common/bl2_plat_setup.c
@@ -238,4 +238,10 @@ void bl2_platform_setup(void)
 	NOTICE("BL2: SYS_LSI_MODE: 0x%x\n", mmio_read_32(SYS_LSI_MODE));
 	NOTICE("BL2: SYS_LSI_DEVID: 0x%x\n", mmio_read_32(SYS_LSI_DEVID));
 	NOTICE("BL2: SYS_LSI_PRR: 0x%x\n", mmio_read_32(SYS_LSI_PRR));
+#ifdef EDGE_BOOT_VERSION
+	NOTICE("[EDGE] BL2   version=%s profile=%s machine=%s\n",
+	       EDGE_BOOT_VERSION, EDGE_BOOT_PROFILE, EDGE_BOOT_MACHINE);
+#else
+	NOTICE("[EDGE] BL2   version=unset\n");
+#endif
 }
